    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d534">

                <pb facs="0649" n="551" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg551"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2867: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-07-15T12:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 15,
                                1920—noon</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>742. Your 1057, July 13, 7 p.m.</p>
                <p>This Government did not feel warranted in communicating to the Japanese
                    Government the British and French Government’s approval of the Lamont-Kajiwara
                        letters<anchor n="44" xml:id="d534-f1"/> but will be glad to communicate <pb
                        facs="0650" n="552" xml:id="pg552"/> such approval if the British and French
                    Governments will authorize it so to do and will instruct their representatives
                    at Tokyo to that effect.</p>
                <p>Repeat to Paris as number 1252.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
